Bugfix: Copy public links with the Clipboard API instead of execCommand

The "Copy to clipboard" button of a public link in the sharing panel copied the
link from an invisible input (a 1px box with the input at width 80%) through
clipboard.js, which uses document.execCommand("copy"). Chromium copies an empty
string from a text input whose content box has zero width, so as soon as a theme
sized that input with box-sizing: border-box the button silently put nothing on
the clipboard. The button now uses the asynchronous Clipboard API where it is
available (secure contexts) and keeps clipboard.js only as the fallback. The
fallback instance is no longer created again on every render, and the feedback
tooltip now shows the "Copied!" message instead of the button title.

